  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Good Lovin'** (1 review): Reviewer singles out this song as a highlight of the recording [3]\n- **Terrapin Station** (1 review): Reviewer names Terrapin as one of the highlights [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **All Along the Wathtower**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **DeadCo2021-10-20.travitz.litz.schoepsCMC64v.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 18 songs; 203 min; rated 4.67/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer hears the performances as loose and exploratory in this recording; Reviewer's own recording sounds nice but not as good as the other posted recordings [3][4]\n- **DeadCo2021-10-20.travitz.litz.schoepsCMC64v.flac24**: source not stated; 18 songs; 203 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer says it was their first Dead show in Colorado [4]\n- Jay Lane sat in for Bill Kreutzmann at this show [1]\n- Jay Lane sat in for Bill Kreutzmann at this show [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **DeadCo2021-10-20.travitz.litz.schoepsCMC64v.flac16**: taped by Jeff Travitz; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Schoeps CMC64v's>Grace Design Lunatec V3>Sound Devices 744t [1]. Also: Reviewer also recorded the show, from the eighth row far off to the side; Edited in Sound Forge Pro 15 with fades, POW-r dither to 16-bit/44.1kHz, tracked in CDWAV, FLAC via Trader's Little Helper [1][4]\n- **DeadCo2021-10-20.travitz.litz.schoepsCMC64v.flac24**: taped by Jeff Travitz; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Schoeps CMC64v's>Grace Design Lunatec V3>Sound Devices 744t [2]. Also: 24-bit version: Sound Forge Pro 15 fades only, tracked in CDWAV, FLAC via Trader's Little Helper, tagged in Foobar2000 [2]",
